  "result": "No actions yet; I've already read what I need.\n\n---\n\nI had a look at the site. Right now it builds the timetable page from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, so the site currently has no way of knowing about a cancellation, let alone warning anyone.\n\nThat makes the first thing to settle where the news of a cancellation comes from. It decides most of what I'd build: whether it's a change to the nightly file, a way for someone to flag a sailing during the day, or something else. It also decides how quickly a warning could reach people.\n\n**When a sailing gets cancelled today, how does that happen? Who makes the call, how far ahead, and how do passengers currently find out?**\n\nOr if you'd rather I just dive in, say so.",
